## Background and Motivation

To support Keyed Services in MVC, we need to make a small change to `BindingInfo`.

## Proposed API

```diff
namespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;

public class BindingInfo
{
+    public object? ServiceKey { get; set; }
}
```

## Usage Examples

This property will be set by calling `BindingInfo.GetBindingInfo(IEnumerable<object> attributes)`, like other existing property (`PropertyFilterProvider`, `RequestPredicate`, etc.)

Attributes are already extracted for this method.

## Alternative Designs

Without this property, we will need to do some reflection for all binding that comes from the service provider.

``` csharp
var attribute = context.Metadata.Identity.ParameterInfo?.GetCustomAttribute<FromKeyedServicesAttribute>();
if (attribute?.Key == null)
{
    // existing path
}
else
{
   // keyed service path
}
```
This will be expensive, since it will be done for all parameter that binds from the service provider. 

## Risks

A custom implementation of `IModelBinder` that target `BindingSource.Services` could resolve a non-keyed service when a keyed one was requested if they don't check `BindingInfo.ServiceKey`. But that's also the reason why I think this property needs to be public and not internal.

I don't expect a performance hit since the attributes are already populated when calling `BindingInfo.GetBindingInfo`.

comments:
API Review Notes:

- Is there any place more logical than `BindingInfo` for this?
  - Not that we know of. This allows us to cache the key for the parameter relatively early.
- Should this be internal?
  - While we don't have an exact use case for external users, things like ApiVersioning use BindingInfo, and it would feel like a gap to omit this information when most of the properties are public.

API Approved!

```diff
namespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;

public class BindingInfo
{
+    public object? ServiceKey { get; set; }
}
```
